+* `[ARN-2]` Values allocated in an arena are **not dropped individually**. Consequently, ordinary Arena bulk allocation MUST NOT accept an element type for which `needs_drop(T)` is true, regardless of whether `T` implements `Default`, `Zeroable`, or both. This guarantees that ordinary Arena reclamation never needs per-element destructor execution.
+* `[ARN-3]` Allocating a type that `needs_drop` in an arena is `E3090` unless the call is `alloc_nodrop` (explicit acknowledgement that `drop` will never run) — this keeps arenas free of destructor bookkeeping and prevents silent resource leaks of handles/GPU objects. `alloc_array[T](count)` always requires `!needs_drop(T)` and resolves initialization deterministically: if `T: Zeroable`, it allocates zeroed storage and treats every element as initialized `T`; otherwise, if `T: Default`, it calls `T.default()` once for each element; otherwise it reports the existing unsatisfied-bound diagnostic `E2040`. If both capabilities exist, `Zeroable` takes precedence. That precedence is observable API semantics and MUST NOT be changed by optimization.
